  "duration": 167.6999969482422,
  "text": "Hey, it's TJ again from Hawkeye Camera Systems and we're going to go over a few things about cellular service and connectivity in regards to your Hawkeye camera. So here in my hand is what we call the Omni antenna or Omni directional antenna that comes standard with all Hawkeye camera systems. 95 plus percent of our customers will never have an issue with cell service that is achieved with this antenna, but we'll go forward. So with the camera system, you're going to receive a six foot antenna cable to connect your antenna to the bottom of the camera. This generally needs to be mounted as high as possible on your T-post because height is your friend for cell service. The higher you can get your antenna, the better the chances are of maximum connectivity. So this Omni antenna comes with your camera because it searches for service in a circle 360 degrees all around. But if you are too far away from a cell tower, there's a few things we can do. But generally speaking, if you're within eight or less miles of a cell tower, which is most people, this antenna is plenty enough to achieve great connectivity. In the event that you start to experience some service problems, there's a few things that we recommend. Like I say, the higher you can get this, the better. So one option is a 30 foot antenna cable. This allows you to extend your antenna 30 plus feet in the air with the use of the cable to overcome any topography that may be in the way of your camera to the tower. So if you have a levee or a high hill between your camera and the tower, you can experience connectivity issues. We also have 30 foot extension poles that you can buy at hogeyecameras.com along with this cable to help you out and get you as high in the air as possible. In the event that you are in an extremely remote area, we do have access to provide you with a directional antenna. This is something that 95 plus percent of our customers will never have to worry about because of the amount of cell towers in the United States today. But if you are in one of those rare areas where you're 8, 10 plus miles away from the cell tower, this directional antenna that you can acquire from us can get you connected up to 12 or potentially maybe even more miles away. But anyway, you will probably not have to worry about this, but it is something to keep in mind. If you have any other questions about connectivity and service issues, feel free to call our tech support team anytime.",
